Atlas overlay patch 0023: ui/sidebar-footer
Why: the foot of the sidebar is the "New tab" row with its shortcut in 11 px dim and a rule above it
(reel scene R02, tokens.md section 3). The engine already has a new-tab button at the bottom of the
sidebar (VerticalNewTabButton); this gives it the Atlas label (sentence case, from the sidebar string
part) and draws the rule and the shortcut through chrome/browser/ui/atlas/sidebar/footer_row. A row
with different content needs no new view, so no lower tier than a paint hook exists.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/vertical/vertical_new_tab_button.{h,cc},
 chrome/browser/ui/views/tabs/vertical/BUILD.gn
Test filter: *AtlasSidebar*; journey R02 (footer row)
Rebase risk: L (one small class)
Release: 0.13
License: BSD-3-Clause (hunks in engine files the inherited series does not patch)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

